{"seq":1221,"lane":"B","class":"weak-cpu-revenue-links","severity":"serious","evidence":"1221.json links both “Vera is important because there’s only so much memory that you can put in a single server” and “competitors like OpenAI, with its Jalapeño chip, are trying to sidestep the problem by minimizing data movement altogether” to v7, “What revenue will NVIDIA report from stand-alone CPUs for FY2027?”","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D259: evidence must help answer the linked question through a discernible business path.","mechanism":"B treats general data-orchestration descriptions as evidence for stand-alone CPU revenue, without establishing a connection to CPU sales, pricing or supply."}
{"seq":1221,"lane":"B","class":"excluded-product-comparison","severity":"minor","evidence":"1221.json e3: “By accelerating data operations, Nvidia claims up to 3x improvements in certain workloads”.","rule":"Signed standard §5.3 and D250 boundary 3 exclude a company’s own product-performance comparison unless the passage also contains a separately helpful action.","mechanism":"B retains a company performance claim as CPU-revenue evidence without applying the product-detail exclusion."}
{"seq":1223,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1223.json e4: “I do wonder the extent to which the financial markets have fully priced in Nvidia's financing of their customers” is linked to v1, “Will NVIDIA enter at least one publicly verifiable binding financial guarantee or unsold-capacity purchase commitment under the AI Compute Partnership by 2027-01-31?”","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D207: a statement must help answer the question to which it is filed.","mechanism":"B connects a general valuation concern about customer financing to a specific partnership guarantee, although the speaker says nothing about that partnership or its commitments."}
{"seq":1223,"lane":"B","class":"excluded-product-comparison","severity":"minor","evidence":"1223.json e9: “the chip reportedly delivers 1.5 to 1.9 times more AI work per watt and up to 3.6 times lower latency than Nvidia's GB200/GB300, while consuming half the power”.","rule":"Signed standard §5.3 and D250 boundary 3 exclude third-party product comparisons; a comparison made by the competitor itself is assessed separately.","mechanism":"B files a media-reported performance comparison under total revenue. The separate statement about production and possible competitive pressure is retained as e10."}
{"seq":1223,"lane":"B","class":"lost-forecast-period","severity":"serious","evidence":"1223.json article: “expect roughly 70% sales growth in fiscal 2028 ... and management indicated that without supply constraints, growth would exceed 100%.” B e7 says “the period is not specified.”","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires a record to preserve the period of a forecast.","mechanism":"B extracts the conditional forecast as a separate passage and fails to carry forward the fiscal 2028 period established in the same sentence."}
{"seq":1227,"lane":"A","class":"opening-summary-loses-amount","severity":"serious","evidence":"1227.json e1 quotes “raise its 2026 capital expenditure forecast toward as much as $205 billion” but its stored one-line summary says only “Reports management’s raised 2026 capex forecast and identifies AI and cloud data-center infrastructure as the spending drivers.”","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires the amount and its upper-limit condition to be preserved in a standalone record.","mechanism":"A’s what_it_shows omits the amount and its limit; build_handover copies that field directly into one_line."}
{"seq":1227,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1227.json A e1 and B e2 both quote management’s decision to “raise its 2026 capital expenditure forecast toward as much as $205 billion”; _ledger.json stores them separately as e4278 under v73 and e4279 under v4.","rule":"Signed standard §2 and D250 count one research matter in one article as one record; one record can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B produce separate pieces from the same article, and the writer stores each handover piece separately without reconciling them across the two answers."}
{"seq":1227,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"rung-boundary-mismatch","severity":"serious","evidence":"1227.json v73: the neutral condition says “at most 215250000000 USD” while its numeric hi is 215250000000; the next condition says “above 215250000000 USD” while its lo is 215250000000.","rule":"Signed standard §3 requires outcomes with no gaps or overlaps; META_SYSTEM defines numeric lower bounds as inclusive and upper bounds as exclusive.","mechanism":"check_bounds checks adjacent numeric bounds but does not check that the written conditions agree with them. At exactly $215.25 billion, the text and numeric fields select different outcomes."}
{"seq":1227,"lane":"judging","class":"spending-scope-conflated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1227.json v73 judgement says “The management reference is its FY2026 capex forecast of up to $205 billion, with a reported range of $195–$205 billion”; cited e4288 in _ledger.json says “Alphabet raised its 2026 AI infrastructure spending forecast to a range of $195 billion to $205 billion.”","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires a record and judgement to preserve what a figure measures; §7 requires the conclusion to follow the cited evidence.","mechanism":"The judgement treats a range described as AI infrastructure spending as the range for total company capital expenditure without establishing that the scopes are identical."}
{"seq":1228,"lane":"A","class":"missing-main-driver-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1228.json article: “analysts currently expect fiscal 2027 revenue of 391.1 billion dollars, compared with reported fiscal 2026 revenue of 331.8 billion dollars”; A opens only a question about Azure growth.","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4: a company’s annual main-driver quantity can open when it has independent investment significance and no open question covers it.","mechanism":"A identifies the cloud growth question but does not propose a separate Microsoft total-revenue question despite the article’s full-year company forecast. The trace does not establish why."}
{"seq":1228,"lane":"A","class":"opening-summary-loses-amount","severity":"serious","evidence":"1228.json e1 quotes “revenue increased 43% year-over-year in fiscal Q4 2026” but summarizes it as “strong recent Azure growth”; e2 quotes “about 45% in constant currency in fiscal Q1 2027” but summarizes it as “near-term Azure growth guidance”.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires the amount, period and relevant conditions to be preserved in a standalone record.","mechanism":"A’s summaries omit both growth rates, and build_handover copies what_it_shows directly into the stored one_line fields."}
{"seq":1228,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"currency-basis-ambiguity","severity":"minor","evidence":"1228.json v74 asks for “year-over-year revenue growth” for FY2027, while its comparison is “45% constant-currency Azure growth guidance for fiscal Q1 2027”; the judgement says the evidence does not quantify an adjustment to the eventual reported full-year figure.","rule":"Signed standard §4 requires the measurement scope to be clear; §3 requires the middle outcome to state its comparison.","mechanism":"Record preparation carries a constant-currency quarterly reference into a question that does not specify the currency basis of the annual result."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1221,1222,1223,1224,1225,1226,1227,1228],"classes":{"weak-cpu-revenue-links":1,"excluded-product-comparison":2,"wrong-evidence-home":1,"lost-forecast-period":1,"opening-summary-loses-amount":2,"same-article-evidence-duplicated":1,"rung-boundary-mismatch":1,"spending-scope-conflated":1,"missing-main-driver-question":1,"currency-basis-ambiguity":1}}}